hash are the sharing\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1158:                                           \"Projected record set does not contain a child hash\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1159:                                           {:rule :missing-record, :hash h})))]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1161:                   (emit! e :yin.debruijn/hash h)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1170:                   (when (= h fingerprint)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1172:    (walk fingerprint)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1184:   deterministic gate the storage reader hashes behind, so a wrongly\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1187:   hash recomputation.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1193:    (= :string type) (string? v)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1196:    (or (= :ref type) (= :hash type)) (and (string? v)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1220:   :yin.debruijn/hash — derived from `node-grammar`, so the reader's\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1253:    :string (= v (normalize-nfc v))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1267:   what the writer already guarantees, so no minted hash moves.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1273:        present (disj (set (keys record)) :yin.debruijn/hash)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1309:   {:fingerprint h, :records {h record}} — the inverse of\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1312:   :yin.debruijn/hash; exactly one entity is the :yin.debruijn/root\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1313:   marker and its hash is the fingerprint; every slot must fit its\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1314:   declared shape BEFORE its hash is recomputed — a wrongly typed slot\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1321:   :yin.debruijn/operands must be one vector of hashes. Each record is\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1322:   re-hashed and a disagreement is a\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1323:   :hash-mismatch diagnostic — content addressing is verified at this\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1341:                             (let [h (or (when (contains? facts :yin.de