ey would bind: a reserved name\n   141\t   (Rule R), and any binder that is not a symbol, refused as\n   142\t   `:non-symbol-parameter` with the binder's coarse `:kind`. A keyword\n   143\t   parameter would otherwise write any key into a named kernel's\n   144\t   environment, `:yin.k/store-of` included. `data` is merged into the\n   145\t   refusal. Returns `params`.\"\n   146\t  ([params] (check-params! params {}))\n   147\t  ([params data]\n   148\t   (when-let [p (some #(when (reserved-name? %) %) params)]\n   149\t     (refuse-reserved! :binder p data))\n   150\t   (when-let [p (some #(when-not (symbol? %) %) params)]\n   151\t     (throw (ex-info \"Lambda parameter is not a symbol\"\n   152\t                     (merge data\n   153\t                            {:reason :non-symbol-parameter,\n   154\t                             :kind (values/kind-of p)}))))\n   155\t   params))\n   156\t\n   157\t\n   158\t(defn check-bindings!\n   159\t  \"Refuse a supplied map (an env, a store, a registry) that binds a\n   160\t   reserved name. Returns `m`.\"\n   161\t  [role m]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
